# Cursor Anti-Slop Rules

- When generating commit messages or PR descriptions, never use AI cliché buzzwords:
  - Do not use: "load-bearing", "seam", "quietly", "latent", "survived", "genuine", "robust", "seamless", "delve", "orchestrate".
- Ground all explanations in technical diff facts: specify exact files, functions, and bugs.
- Limit PR summaries to max 2 plain sentences without filler.
